Four more builtin app themes are in and verified.

**New themes in [themes/apps/](themes/apps) — each shipped in the binary, overridable by a user file of the same name:**

- [themes/apps/app-notes.json](themes/apps/app-notes.json) — *Paper Notes*: warm parchment tones, serif (Georgia), soft radius — reading first.
- [themes/apps/app-chat.json](themes/apps/app-chat.json) — *Signal Wave*: cool cyan accents on deep slate, rounded bubbles.
- [themes/apps/app-vault.json](themes/apps/app-vault.json) — *Iron Vault*: austere steel grey, 2px radius, top border — reads as secure.
- [themes/apps/app-store.json](themes/apps/app-store.json) — *Market Green*: fresh green install buttons.

**The Store needed one wiring change:** the store isn't a module, it's an overlay, so its theme key is `app-store` and [app.rs](crates/mandala-shell/src/app.rs) now targets it whenever `store_open` is set — the store (even opened over a running app) always shows Market Green, and back restores the previous context's theme. Theme files for the other 13 slots (weather, rss, tasks, …) now follow with zero further code: name one after its id and it lights up.

**Checks run:** `cargo fmt --check` clean · `cargo test --workspace` — 114 passed, 0 failed (test now asserts all six builtin app ids resolve) · Android `cargo ndk -t arm64-v8a build --lib` exit 0. One catch fixed along the way: the store manifest initially carried a stray alpha byte in `surface_primary` (`#12191534`), which the validator would have accepted as 20%-opaque — caught on review and corrected before a build ran.

