All nine plan items are done and verified. Here's the full report.

## What was built (the rice phase)

**Wallpaper-derived theming** — new [palette.rs](crates/mandala-core/src/palette.rs): thumbs the image to 64px, builds a 4096-bucket histogram, picks the most-frequent *saturated* bucket (grey wallpapers fall back to plain frequency) and emits an ordinary `ThemeManifest` (accent/CTA from the wallpaper, canvas forced near-black, CTA label chosen by WCAG contrast). It resolves through `ThemeManifest::resolve()` before being written, so a bad derivation fails the command instead of shipping an unloadable theme. `wallpaper <path>` now works on desktop too: derive → write `themes/wallpaper-derived.json` → persist `wallpaper.path` → select + repaint; Android additionally sets the system wallpaper via JNI. Both restore on the next boot (shell [lib.rs](crates/mandala-shell/src/lib.rs)).

**Rice UI** — wallpaper `Image` layer (`cover`) behind everything in [main_window.slint](crates/mandala-ui/ui/main_window.slint); waybar-style status bar with context / theme / install-count / live clock pills (`BarPill` in [components.slint](crates/mandala-ui/ui/components.slint), 1s `slint::Timer`); two new presets `hypr-rice` and `kitty`; motion (180ms workspace glide on app open/close, rail/drawer slides, 150ms overlay fades — rails/drawers/overlays now stay mounted so both directions animate, with focus gates carrying the visibility state).

**Shortcuts** — Ctrl+Space focuses the command bar, Ctrl+T opens the terminal, from any workspace focus state; button scopes reject modifier chords so chords bubble instead of "clicking", while plain Space still activates. Tested headlessly in [shortcuts.rs](crates/mandala-ui/tests/shortcuts.rs).

**Docs** — [design-system.md](docs/design-system.md) gained a "Rice layer" section plus updated timing/keyboard rules.

## Fixes along the way

- Borrow-check error in `palette.rs` (closure capturing `best` mutably) → extracted a `consider(&mut best, …)` fn.
- `theme::tests::selection` walked the preset cycle and wasn't updated for the two new presets → extended to the 6-theme cycle.
- My test helper tapped Ctrl *before* the key (modifier already released when the key arrived) → `ctrl_chord` now holds Control across the tap; also renamed the helper that was shadowed by the parameter name.

## Verification (actually run)

- `cargo fmt --check` — clean.
- `cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast` — **exit 0, 123 passed, 0 failed** (100 core + 11 shell + 7 + both headless UI tests; 1 ignored).
- `cargo ndk -t arm64-v8a build --lib -p mandala-shell --features android` — **exit 0**, linked `libmandala_shell.so` for arm64-v8a.
- `cargo run -p mandala-shell -- --selftest` — passed, 6 signed modules load.

## Limitations

- No visual screenshot check: this environment has no compositor/display (same gap as prior sessions), so the rice look was verified by compile + tests, not pixels.
- The Android JNI wallpaper path still needs an on-device smoke test (needs adb/a device).
- Deviation from the plan: Ctrl+Return is *not* wired — Slint's single-line TextInput consumes Return (fires `accepted`) before window scopes see it, so it could only work outside the command bar. Ctrl+T is the terminal chord from every focus state; this is recorded as a `shortcut:` note in the doc.

